title: Initials
golf: 55

Write `initials(name)` that returns the first letter of each name, each followed by a dot.
`initials("Ada Lovelace")` gives `"A.L."`.
=== starter
def initials(name):
    ...
=== broken
def initials(name):
    return ".".join(word[0] for word in name.split())
=== test
from harness import eq


def test_initials(sol):
    eq(sol.initials("Ada Lovelace"), "A.L.", 'initials("Ada Lovelace")')
    eq(sol.initials("Guido van Rossum"), "G.v.R.", 'initials("Guido van Rossum")')
